{"total_count":8,"incomplete_results":false,"items":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/74","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/74/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/74/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/74/events","html_url":"https://github.com/lukaslueg/built/issues/74","id":2697747030,"node_id":"I_kwDOBOZo0M6gzFpW","number":74,"title":"`FEATURES_LOWERCASE` contains features that do not exists","user":{"login":"barakugav","id":15381794,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MzgxNzk0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15381794?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/barakugav","html_url":"https://github.com/barakugav","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barakugav/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barakugav/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barakugav/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barakugav/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barakugav/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barakugav/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barakugav/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barakugav/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/barakugav/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2024-11-27T09:04:20Z","updated_at":"2024-12-06T12:51:20Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"The `FEATURES_LOWERCASE` static variable is created by searching for env variables with prefix `CARGO_FEATURE_`, and parsing the suffixes to extract features names.\r\nIts correct that every feature has such env variable, but not each such env variable is a real enabled feature.\r\nFor example, when I compile my executable I get these additional features that are not part of my crate:\r\n```rust\r\n\"libc\", \"numpy\", \"pyo3\"\r\n```\r\nI can't say why these environment variables were on, but its not due to exports in `bashrc` or something like that, probably env variables manipulations by my dependencies build scripts.\r\nAnyway, I think a better approach is to parse `Cargo.toml` and extract all of the possible features of the current built crate, and than check if there is an env variable called `format!(CARGO_FEATURE_{}\", feature.to_uppercase().replace(\"-\", \"_\"))`.\r\n\r\nThis is how I do it in my `build.rs`:\r\n```rust\r\nfn enabled_features() -> Vec<String> {\r\n    let cargo_toml = Path::new(&env!(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")).join(\"Cargo.toml\");\r\n    fs::read_to_string(cargo_toml)\r\n        .expect(\"Failed to read Cargo.toml\")\r\n        .parse::<toml::Table>()\r\n        .expect(\"Failed to parse Cargo.toml\")\r\n        .into_iter()\r\n        .flat_map(|features| {\r\n            features\r\n                .as_table()\r\n                .expect(\"features must be a table\")\r\n                .keys()\r\n                .filter(|k| *k != \"default\")\r\n                .cloned()\r\n        })\r\n        .filter(|f| {\r\n            env::var(format!(\r\n                \"CARGO_FEATURE_{}\",\r\n                f.to_uppercase().replace(\"-\", \"_\")\r\n            ))\r\n            .is_ok()\r\n        })\r\n        .collect()\r\n}\r\n```","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/74/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/74/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/72","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/72/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/72/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/72/events","html_url":"https://github.com/lukaslueg/built/issues/72","id":2624849896,"node_id":"I_kwDOBOZo0M6cdAfo","number":72,"title":"Support for customizing the BUILT_TIME_UTC format","user":{"login":"vstojkovic-mongodb","id":90724588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNzI0NTg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/90724588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vstojkovic-mongodb","html_url":"https://github.com/vstojkovic-mongodb","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vstojkovic-mongodb/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vstojkovic-mongodb/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vstojkovic-mongodb/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vstojkovic-mongodb/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vstojkovic-mongodb/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vstojkovic-mongodb/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vstojkovic-mongodb/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vstojkovic-mongodb/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vstojkovic-mongodb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2024-10-30T17:40:04Z","updated_at":"2024-11-04T10:03:39Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Would it be possible to add an option that controls how the `BUILT_TIME_UTC` string is formatted?","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/72/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/72/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/57","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/57/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/57/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/57/events","html_url":"https://github.com/lukaslueg/built/issues/57","id":1857441736,"node_id":"I_kwDOBOZo0M5utk_I","number":57,"title":"Chrono feature in built_time() example on docs.rs","user":{"login":"trebinor","id":2577124,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NzcxMjQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2577124?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/trebinor","html_url":"https://github.com/trebinor","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trebinor/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trebinor/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trebinor/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trebinor/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trebinor/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trebinor/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trebinor/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trebinor/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/trebinor/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":10,"created_at":"2023-08-19T00:54:03Z","updated_at":"2023-08-21T20:23:43Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"An example function built_time() appears for the latest (0.6.1) version of built on docs.rs\r\n\r\n```\r\n#[cfg(feature = \"chrono\")]\r\nfn built_time() -> built::chrono::DateTime<built::chrono::Local> {\r\n    built::util::strptime(built_info::BUILT_TIME_UTC)\r\n        .with_timezone(&built::chrono::offset::Local)\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhat is the proper way to enable the chrono feature to enable conditional compilation of built_time()?  Maybe this cfg is no longer needed, because commenting it out includes the function.  Note that that adding this to Cargo.toml has no effect.\r\n```\r\n[features]\r\nchrono = []\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe fix can be tested by adding built_time() before main() in built/example_project/src/main.rs and adding this to main():\r\n\r\n```\r\n    println!(\"Build time: {:?}\", built_time());\r\n```\r\nYou should see that built_time() is not found when the cfg is present, and the build succeeds if it's commented out.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/57/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/57/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/55","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/55/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/55/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/55/events","html_url":"https://github.com/lukaslueg/built/issues/55","id":1710781025,"node_id":"I_kwDOBOZo0M5l-HJh","number":55,"title":"Filter dependencies by feature, target, and kind","user":{"login":"jwodder","id":98207,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4MjA3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98207?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwodder","html_url":"https://github.com/jwodder","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwodder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwodder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwodder/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwodder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwodder/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwodder/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwodder/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwodder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jwodder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2023-05-15T20:30:48Z","updated_at":"2023-09-09T12:53:26Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Currently, it appears that `built` determines the value of `DEPENDENCIES` by just parsing `Cargo.lock` and extracting the name & version of every entry.  This strikes me as suboptimal, as presumably one would want the list of dependencies stored in a binary to match the actual dependencies used to build it, i.e., excluding dev dependencies, dependencies for other targets, and dependencies for inactive features.\r\n\r\nAs `built` currently doesn't do such filtering, [I implemented it myself in my own `build.rs`](https://github.com/jwodder/confab/blob/393807ca4f2280a8a1118a29654503a4afe6f604/build.rs#L132) by using `cargo-metadata` and traversing the \"resolve\" nodes; feel free to make use of this MIT-licensed code if you need it.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/55/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/55/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/40","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/40/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/40/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/40/events","html_url":"https://github.com/lukaslueg/built/issues/40","id":913511301,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU5MTM1MTEzMDE=","number":40,"title":"Add support for CARGO_CFG_TARGET_FEATURE","user":{"login":"akanalytics","id":14971538,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTcxNTM4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14971538?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanalytics","html_url":"https://github.com/akanalytics","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanalytics/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanalytics/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanalytics/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanalytics/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanalytics/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanalytics/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanalytics/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanalytics/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akanalytics/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2021-06-07T12:48:12Z","updated_at":"2021-06-07T15:41:28Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Would it be possible to add support for CARGO_CFG_TARGET_FEATURE. Typical example might be \"mmx,sse\"\r\nThis would allow programs to report on how optimized they are for various processors (using SIMD instructions etc). \r\nWould be useful for chess engines written in rust :-) ","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/40/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/40/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/22","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/22/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/22/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/22/events","html_url":"https://github.com/lukaslueg/built/issues/22","id":522438082,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU1MjI0MzgwODI=","number":22,"title":"Add target-cpu value?","user":{"login":"novacrazy","id":4708645,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDg2NDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4708645?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/novacrazy","html_url":"https://github.com/novacrazy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/novacrazy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/novacrazy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/novacrazy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/novacrazy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/novacrazy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/novacrazy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/novacrazy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/novacrazy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/novacrazy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2019-11-13T19:55:00Z","updated_at":"2020-08-18T18:38:38Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I have an application that will be distributed for specific CPU models in order to take advantage of specific instructions and different techniques better suited for AMD or Intel. \r\n\r\nIt would be nice to have `built` parse `RUSTFLAGS` and store `target-cpu` so it could be included in the build information.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/22/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/22/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/19","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/19/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/19/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/19/events","html_url":"https://github.com/lukaslueg/built/issues/19","id":411667131,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0MTE2NjcxMzE=","number":19,"title":"Automatically rebuild if Cargo.toml or git changes","user":{"login":"tylerhawkes","id":7120045,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxMjAwNDU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7120045?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerhawkes","html_url":"https://github.com/tylerhawkes","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerhawkes/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerhawkes/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerhawkes/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerhawkes/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerhawkes/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerhawkes/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerhawkes/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerhawkes/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tylerhawkes/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2019-02-18T22:20:25Z","updated_at":"2025-05-01T18:13:43Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Of all the things that are recorded by built, Cargo.toml and git can change without triggering a rebuild the next time `cargo build` is run. If those options are enabled, built should emit `cargo:rerun-if-changed=<file>` for the Cargo.toml and any files in .git. That way cargo can automatically determine if the build.sh script needs to rerun or not. \r\nI ran into this issue trying to do a manual release (we're working on CI) of an internal project and had to manually change the build.rs file to get cargo to rerun built and get a new git hash.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/19/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/19/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/5","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/5/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/5/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/5/events","html_url":"https://github.com/lukaslueg/built/issues/5","id":252647490,"node_id":"MDU6SXNzdWUyNTI2NDc0OTA=","number":5,"title":"Add support for accessing `Cargo.toml` values","user":{"login":"daniel-abramov","id":2765698,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NjU2OTg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2765698?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-abramov","html_url":"https://github.com/daniel-abramov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-abramov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-abramov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-abramov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-abramov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-abramov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-abramov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-abramov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-abramov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/daniel-abramov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2017-08-24T15:52:11Z","updated_at":"2023-01-09T22:18:16Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Currently some of the values like crate version or crate name are already present in the generated file, however not all of values are present.\r\n\r\nWhat I would like to suggest is to create some sort of the config, which contains every field from `Cargo.toml`, i.e. to use `toml` and `serde-derive` to parse the `Cargo.toml` and store in an appropriate structure.\r\n\r\nWhen the user needs some values from `Cargo.toml`, such approach would allow the users to inspect the content of `Cargo.toml` which was used for the crate when it was built.\r\n\r\nI encountered this issue today: there are several values defined inside `Cargo.toml` in `[package.metadata.bundle]` section, and I would like to be able to access the values from the code.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/5/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/lukaslueg/built/issues/5/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}